    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0305" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1039"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Gibbs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                        1879</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 129.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your Nos. 215 and 268 touching
                    the claim of Thomas W. Sparrow on Peru, I have to observe that Mr. C. G. Lee,
                    attorney for claimant, has lately addressed the Department, urging that the
                    matter be pressed on the attention of the Peruvian Government. I have informed
                    him that your last dispatch on the subject gave reason to suppose that the claim
                    would soon be settled.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. M. Evarts.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
